<Docs title="Documentation"><div class="doc-title"><span class="section-kicker">AGENTGUARD / DOCUMENTATION</span><h1>Build an explicit<br/>authorization boundary.</h1><p>Start with a working local policy. Then choose your integration and make its trust boundaries visible.</p></div><h2>Build and operate</h2><div class="docs-grid">{guides.map(([path,title,body])=><a class="docs-card" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}docs/${path}/`}><h2>{title} ↗</h2><p>{body}</p></a>)}</div><h2>Project status</h2><p>These guides map to the checked-in release surface. The security model and production guide state the supported topology and the boundaries that remain operator-managed. See <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md">the changelog</a>, <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/SUPPORT.md">support policy</a>, and <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/SECURITY.md">security response process</a>.</p></Docs>
